# M1 — Gateway keeps 5 minutes of a take

A device's request window holds up to 305 s of audio instead of 60 s, and a cut window is logged, never silent.

**Scope.** `gateway/src/hermes_gateway/session.py` (`MIC_CAP_SAMPLES`, `DeviceSession.handle_binary`),
`gateway/tests/test_session.py`, `protocol/protocol.md` (one sentence in the request window section — no
message, schema or example changes). Memory: 305 s × 16 kHz × 2 B ≈ 9.8 MB per open window, one per device.

## Tasks

| Task | Description | Files | SP | Status |
|------|-------------|-------|----|--------|
| 1.1 | Replace `MIC_CAP_SAMPLES = 60 * audio.RATE` with `MAX_TAKE_S = 300`, `MIC_CAP_SAMPLES = (MAX_TAKE_S + 5) * audio.RATE`; in `handle_binary`, when a frame would pass the cap, log `device %s: request %s cut at %d s` once per `_Mic` (a `cut: bool` field on `_Mic`) | `gateway/src/hermes_gateway/session.py` | 1 | pending |
| 1.2 | Tests: a window fed 290 s of PCM frames keeps all of them (the STT fake receives 290 s); one fed 320 s keeps exactly 305 s and logs the cut once | `gateway/tests/test_session.py` | 1 | pending |
| 1.3 | `protocol/protocol.md`: state in the `request.start`/binary frame section that a request window holds at most 305 s of audio and the gateway drops the rest (logged); the device caps takes at 300 s | `protocol/protocol.md` | 0 | pending |

