# M3 — Core: a take survives the background

When the app goes to the background during a take, the microphone keeps delivering and the gateway link stays up until the take ends; then the devices stop and the 3-min hold starts.

**Scope.** `client/cmd/petcore/core.go` (`core` struct, `SetForeground`, `pump`), `client/cmd/petcore/core_test.go`.
No change to `client/internal/audio`.

## Tasks

| Task | Description | Files | SP | Status |
|------|-------------|-------|----|--------|
| 3.1 | Add `listening atomic.Bool` (set in `pump` on every `voice.StateChanged`) and `deferred atomic.Bool`; `SetForeground(false)`: `background=true`, `runner.SetBackground(true)`, then if `listening` set `deferred` and log `android: background during a take, the microphone stays open`, else `stopDevices()` + `host.Pause(app.HoldAfter)` as today | `client/cmd/petcore/core.go` | 1 | pending |
| 3.2 | New `core.takeEnded()` called from `pump` when the state leaves `StateListening`: if `background && deferred.CompareAndSwap(true,false)` → `stopDevices()`, `host.Pause(app.HoldAfter)`, log `android: take ended in the background`; `SetForeground(true)` clears `deferred` before `startDevices()` (no double start: `startDevices` stays idempotent as the gate is) | `client/cmd/petcore/core.go` | 1 | pending |
| 3.3 | Tests: background while listening → `stopped == 0`, `h.paused == 0`; a `StateChanged{Thinking}` then → `stopped == 1`, `h.paused == 1`, `h.after == app.HoldAfter`; background while listening then foreground before the take ends → no stop, no pause, `deferred` false; `TestLifecycleParksAndUnparks` unchanged | `client/cmd/petcore/core_test.go` | 1 | pending |

